Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "WetRoadNightScene" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :EvidenceBasedAnomaly ;
    :hasEvidence :evidence1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 .

:evidence1 a :RollingBallIndicator ;
    :description "Reflective water on road surface indicating wet conditions" ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :risk1 .

:weather1 a :RainyCondition ;
    :description "Nighttime scene with wet road surface" .

:risk1 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Reduced traction due to wet road surface" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Limited visibility due to nighttime and potential rain" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential rear-end collision due to reduced visibility and braking distance" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.60"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.80"^^xsd:float .

:trafficLight1 a :TrafficLight ;
    :description "Visible traffic light showing red" ;
    :occursInScene :scene1 .

:trafficSign1 a :TrafficSign ;
    :description "No entry sign visible on the right" ;
    :occursInScene :scene1 .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

**Risk 1:**
Description: Reduced traction due to wet road surface
Severity Score: 0.75

**Risk 2:**
Description: Limited visibility due to nighttime and potential rain
Severity Score: 0.60

**Risk 3:**
Description: Potential rear-end collision due to reduced visibility and braking distance
Severity Score: 0.80

---
The scene was classified as an **EvidenceBasedAnomaly** due to the rolling ball indicator (reflective water on the road surface) suggesting wet conditions. The identified risks include **RoadConditionRisk** (wet road), **OcclusionRisk** (limited visibility), and **CollisionRisk** (rear-end collision). The severity scores reflect the potential danger of these conditions in a nighttime driving scenario.